{"agent_id":"pp3g-GVZT-open-ended-architectural-review-on-issue-370-read-the","agent_seq":3,"timestamp":"2026-08-14T23:51:19.888579508Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ac9ff902-e363-4e7a-be69-4fbadf893f69","comment_uuid":"7ca4f4ed-4f28-4e44-b6ff-98705e5c2e92","author":"pp3g-GVZT-open-ended-architectural-review-on-issue-370-read-the","content":"# ARCHITECTURAL VERDICT — Tools/Monorepo Drift\n\n**VERDICT: The current architecture is FUNDAMENTALLY FLAWED. The drift problem is INHERENT to the distribution model. I recommend extending the crosslink binary to embed plugins/wrappers, making crosslink the SINGLE DISTRIBUTION CHANNEL for all shared artifacts.**\n\n## EVIDENCE VERIFIED\n\n**Drift confirmed:**\n- Guard plugins: ASES 42.1K / tripn 37.6K / Tools 33.5K (200 lines behind)\n- Wrappers: live claude 86L vs Tools 71L; live opencode 100L vs Tools 54L (missing #274 guard)\n- Model plugins: Tools/plugin.ts 51L BEHIND deployed 133L (missing #347 grok-ban)\n- plugin.ts vs dynamic-models.ts near-duplicates already diverged\n- hook-config precedence bug: LIVE BUG affecting orchestrator git merge\n- .claude/hooks+commands+mcp are gitignored snapshots (confirmed in .gitignore) — no canonical git source\n\n**Distribution model:**\n- Crosslink binary embeds hooks/skills/commands/mcp/rules → deploys via `crosslink init`\n- Tools holds plugins/wrappers/skills → distributed via manual copy or proposed sync-tooling.sh\n- TWO OVERLAPPING DISTRIBUTION CHANNELS create split-brain problem\n\n## ANALYSIS\n\n**(a) Is warehouse + copy-out sound?** NO. Copy/drift is INHERENT when multiple consumers maintain independent copies with no mechanical enforcement. The proposed sync-tooling.sh + drift markers is REACTIVE (detects drift after it occurs), not PREVENTIVE.\n\n**(b) Better distribution mechanism?** YES. Six alternatives considered. RECOMMENDATION: crosslink binary embeds EVERYTHING (plugins/wrappers in addition to hooks/skills/commands/mcp/rules). This provides SINGLE DISTRIBUTION CHANNEL, makes drift STRUCTURALLY IMPOSSIBLE, leverages existing crosslink init mechanism.\n\n**(c) Should layers be separate repos?** Repo-of-repos is NOT the root cause but AMPLIFIES the problem. Single monorepo would eliminate distribution problem but is LARGE STRUCTURAL CHANGE. RECOMMENDATION: keep current repo structure, fix distribution model.\n\n**(d) Consumer-side drift detection right?** NO. It's REACTIVE (smoke detector). BETTER: make drift STRUCTURALLY IMPOSSIBLE via single source of truth (binary embedding) + atomic updates (binary rebuild + init) + no local edits.\n\n**(e) What would I build?** Extend crosslink binary to embed plugins/wrappers. Tools becomes development repo (not distribution). Consumer repos read-only for shared artifacts. Layer-specific customization via hook-config.json.\n\n## MUST CHANGE\n\n1. **Extend crosslink binary to embed plugins/wrappers**: Single distribution channel for all shared artifacts\n2. **Fix hook-config precedence bug**: LIVE BUG — by_type.orchestrator overrides must win over agent_overrides\n3. **Resolve model-plugin duplication**: Merge plugin.ts/dynamic-models.ts (near-duplicates already diverged)\n4. **Document three-class ownership map**: Binary-embedded / layer-owned / machine-local\n\n## SHOULD CONSIDER\n\n1. Stale models-cache.json regeneration mechanism\n2. freeZenModels whitelist update procedure\n3. Tools as development repo (not distribution)\n4. Consumer repos read-only for shared artifacts\n5. Layer-specific customization via hook-config.json\n\n## COMPARISON TO PROPOSED FIX\n\n**Proposed (sync-tooling.sh + drift markers):** REACTIVE enforcement on broken model. Adds detection layer but doesn't fix root cause. Complex (sync script, state machine, --promote flag). Not atomic (later-repo failure leaves earlier repos changed).\n\n**My recommendation:** FIXES THE MODEL. Single distribution channel (crosslink binary). Atomic updates (binary rebuild + init). Drift structurally impossible. Simpler (no sync script, no markers, no state machine). Leverages proven crosslink init mechanism.\n\n**Why mine is better:** Eliminates root cause, simpler, atomic, proven, consistent. Proposed fix is BAND-AID; mine is CURE.\n\n## WHAT-NOT-TESTED\n\n- Crosslink binary extension feasibility (bloat, build complexity) not verified\n- Crosslink init performance with increased artifact set not tested\n- Development workflow (edit in Tools, rebuild crosslink, redeploy) acceptability not validated\n- Layer-specific customization via hook-config.json sufficiency not investigated\n- Hook-config precedence bug fix not executed (design, not verified)\n- plugin.ts/dynamic-models.ts merge strategy not designed\n\n## CONCLUSION\n\nCurrent architecture FUNDAMENTALLY FLAWED. Drift INHERENT to distribution model. Proposed sync-tooling.sh is REACTIVE enforcement on broken model. RECOMMENDATION: extend crosslink binary to embed plugins/wrappers, making crosslink SINGLE DISTRIBUTION CHANNEL. This eliminates root cause, simplifies architecture, makes drift structurally impossible.","created_at":"2026-08-14T23:51:19.882884812Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:cZZ/YTNs/76tDNnwFI4RhYudRZD4zdZqQ3HkqQkWsCs","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg43jB5P36Q6Lo4BeXwyz5Is38CGrbnafi6kZF7JgpLOMAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAJlK+LXf8w8NsSYrgNQh+zB4hnwcC0EO1kXNSPbZ+3ymSXnz2E6XquvhCKbD4p5SbCK4iBSVkETrCYfRIa8HMAw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:cZZ/YTNs/76tDNnwFI4RhYudRZD4zdZqQ3HkqQkWsCs","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg43jB5P36Q6Lo4BeXwyz5Is38CGrbnafi6kZF7JgpLOMAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNK92wZ7loOdzAb0UKS2tZHvEzZa5KN9j/I7iqRmKawWg/oxaXRXZe0mkC/j25SM2OJAUZ6414N3c5hV7Aq8xQM="}
